text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "2000", "image": "", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: Thank you for coming in, Ms. Lenard. I'm Boris Brody. Did you have any trouble finding the office?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Not at all. It's nice to meet you, Mr. Brody.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: You too, Ms. Lenard. Please, take a seat.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Thank you. You have a lovely office.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: Thanks. Alright, let's get down to brass tacks. Please, tell me a little bit about yourself, Kristi.<br />", "id": 1}, {"time": "31000", "image": "", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: I graduated from the English program at Harvard University. I took a variety of courses to ensure I developed the skills I needed in addition to gaining a plethora of knowledge.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: Great. What were some of the courses you took?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: I took a few literature courses, writing and creative writing. I also took quite a few courses in publishing.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: Uh huh.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: I also took some courses that were more hands-on and I am familiar with many of the leading software packages, particularly <span class=\"italic\">inPrint</span>.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: We use <span class=\"italic\">inPrint</span> for layout here too.<br />", "id": 2}, {"time": "64500", "image": "", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: And, in my internship at Polygon, I got to apply many of these skills.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: Good. So in what ways did you benefit from that experience?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Well, even though my responsibilities as an intern were limited, it was a great opportunity to participate and work with a team of professionals. Occasionally there was a crisis and I had to meet deadlines and deal with heavy workloads.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: I see.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: I also had a good working relationship with my boss. We quickly established a good rapport.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Boris</span>: That gives me a good idea of your experience.  Let's move on.<br />", "id": 3}], "video_src": "engenn9le16ob06re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "So Far, So Good! "}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Causatives Get and Have"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use a causative verb when we want to talk about something that someone else did for us. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"strong\">get/have</span> when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Get </span> usually means \"to convince to do something\" or \"to trick someone into doing something\"."}, {"type": "text", "content": "[get + person + to + verb]"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>My boss <span class=\"strong\">got her to work</span> late on Tuesday. </li> <li> Did the boss <span class=\"strong\">get you to work</span> on Saturday?</li></ul> </span>(My boss convinced these people to do something) <br> <br> [get + object + past participle] <br> For example:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li> I had to <span class=\"strong\">get the work done</span> on time.</li></ul>  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have </span></br>{have + object + verb} or {have + object + past participle} "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have</span>  means to give someone the responsibility to do something.<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Dr. Smith <span class=\"strong\">had his nurse take</span> the patient's temperature. </li><li>Please<span class=\"strong\"> have your secretary fax </span>me the information.</li></ul></span></li><li><span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">had the windows washed</span>.</span></li></ul> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you use<span class=\"italic\"> get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My professor got me to take some courses."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We got our workers to use inPrint for layout here too. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " My supervisor had me apply many of these skills. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There was a crisis and my boss had me help in. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are<span class=\"italic\"> used to help us focus on a particular part of the sentence and to emphasise what we want to say by introducing it as a relative clause.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are usually linked to the clause that we want to focus on with <span class=\"strong\">is</span> or <span class=\"strong\">was</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare:    <ul>       <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span> I am looking for is a new secretary.    </br>       A new secretary is <span class=\"strong\">what I</span> am looking for.</ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are often used with verbs like <span class=\"strong\">adore</span>, <span class=\"strong\">dislike</span>, <span class=\"strong\">enjoy</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hate</span>, <span class=\"strong\">like</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hope</span>, <span class=\"strong\">love</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need</span>, <span class=\"strong\">prefer</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">want</span>.<ul><span class=\"strong\">What</span> I<span class=\"strong\"> hate</span> most about going to a job interview is the waiting.      </br>   <span class=\"strong\">   What</span> I<span class=\"strong\"> liked</span> most about their company was the people.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "What-clauses are also often used with <span class=\"strong\">does/do/did </span>and when we want to give emphasis to the whole sentence, rather than a particular clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare:       <ul>   <span class=\"italic\"> The manager interviewed all the salespeople first.  </br><span class=\"strong\">         What </span>the manager <span class=\"strong\">did</span> first <span class=\"strong\">was</span> interview all           the salespeople.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "These sentences are useful in writing where we cannot use intonation for emphasis, but they are also often used in speech."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now what we are looking for is an editorial assistant. I have your letter of reference from your former editor and what she has to say is very complementary. What I hoped to achieve by doing that was to ensure that I developed the skills I needed while gaining a plethora of knowledge."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "get down to brass tacks"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "get to the point quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Alright, let's get down to brass tacks. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when we are talking about our capabilities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "establish a good rapport"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "work together on friendly terms"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My boss and I quickly established a good rapport. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "working relationship"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way two people work together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I had a good working relationship with my boss."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hands-on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "practical; not theoretical"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My professor got me to take some courses that were more hands-on."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "meet deadlines"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "complete work at the expected time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Occasionally, there was a crisis and my boss had to help me in meet deadlines."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm proper interview etiquette."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a poster displaying my ideas in a creative concept."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain why I think certain dos and don'ts are very important."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, brainstorm all the things people should do in an interview and all the things people shouldn't do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Establish which are the most important."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster for the wall with pictures of job interview \u2018dos' and job interview \u2018don'ts'."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Get your pictures from the internet or magazines and make a collage."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Display the posters around the room."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With your partner, make a short presentation explaining your poster."}]}]}